  "preamble": "The shift from the voiceless uvular stop [q] to the glottal stop [ʔ] is a defining characteristic of many modern urban Arabic dialects. This change marks a significant reduction in the place of articulation from the back of the mouth to the throat. In Huanca (Wanka) Quechua, Proto-Quechuan *q became a glottal stop (*piʧqa > piʧʔa 'five').",
